From 294823e7187088c24748c1095a0fdaaa023e8b1c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeff Queisser <funkzy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:42:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 14/16] wifi: apple: centauri: Read the firmware's channel list
 and capabilities

The firmware owns the radio's channel list, its per-country rules and
its capabilities; the driver registered a fixed 2.4/5 GHz table and
never asked. Read the firmware's two reports once the interface is
configured: system command 19, the channels the hardware supports, and
system command 8, the system capabilities. Both are kept as read in
debugfs (ieee80211/phyN/hw_channels and system_caps) and their sizes are
logged. The band table is built from them next.

command() gains a reply buffer, command_reply(): the payload of the
reply to the command that asked is copied there, in place of the ring
consumer's per-command copies. query_link_status() parses the interface
status reply (20) from it; the copy of the country reply (10), which
nothing requested, goes.

Signed-off-by: Jeff Queisser <funkzy@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>

